  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(6, 14, 40)\n\n(10, 14, 48)\n\n**Logic:** [{(First no.) + (Second no.)} × 2]\n\n**(6, 14, 40) →**\n\n⇒ [(6 + 14) × 2]\n\n⇒ (20 × 2) = 40\n\n**(10, 14, 48) →**\n\n⇒ [(10 + 14) × 2]\n\n⇒ (24 × 2) = 48\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1. **(11, 5, 87) →\n\n⇒ [(11 + 5) × 2]\n\n⇒ (16 × 2) = 32\n\n**2. (5, 9, 28) →**\n\n⇒ [(5 + 9) × 2]\n\n⇒ (14 × 2) = **28**\n\n**3. **(5, 6, 45) →\n\n⇒ [(5 + 6) × 2]\n\n⇒ (11 × 2) = 22\n\n**4.** (10, 5, 91) →\n\n⇒ [(10 + 5) × 2]\n\n⇒ (12 × 2) = 30\n\nHere, (5, 9, 28) shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (2)\".",
